      "explanation": "Group the factors with the same base. Multiplying powers with the same base adds their exponents, so\n\\[\n4^4\\cdot9^4\\cdot4^9\\cdot9^9\n=4^{4+9}\\cdot9^{4+9}\n=4^{13}\\cdot9^{13}.\n\\]\nThe two remaining powers have the same exponent. Using \\(a^n b^n=(ab)^n\\), the product becomes\n\\[\n(4\\cdot9)^{13}=\\boxed{36^{13}},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\text{C}\\).",
      "id": "combine_powers",
